  "narration": {
    "title": "The Padres Ran the Table, and It Shows",
    "intro": "Two teams went 6-0 this week for very different reasons. San Diego jumped eleven spots to eighth on a perfect week, while the Dodgers slid past Milwaukee at the top. Here's the state of things around the league.",
    "power_lead": "The Dodgers claimed the top spot at 90-58 after a 5-1 week and a plus-22 run differential, with Max Muncy going 11-for-23 with two homers. But the loudest move belonged to San Diego, up eleven to eighth on a 6-0 sweep behind Jackson Merrill's 11-for-24, three-homer, 10-RBI week. Detroit made the same eleven-spot leap on a 4-2 run, plus-12 for the week.",
    "offense_lead": "The Cubs lead the team-OPS board at .771, a hair ahead of the Dodgers at .757, with Washington and Milwaukee packed in behind. Nothing separating the middle of that pack by much, but Chicago's bats are the deepest going.",
    "staffs_lead": "The Yankees own the best rotation by starter ERA at 3.33, and Cam Schlittler is the reason it reads that way, sitting second among elite arms at a 2.01 ERA. Detroit's staff ranks second at 3.52, quiet company for a team still under .500."
  }
